<meta type=article>
  <title | Appendices>
  <author | Enscribe>
</meta>

<config number-sections=true />

<section | Main body>

An article carries appendices in its back matter, after the body. With section
numbering on, the body sections number 1, 2, … and the appendices are lettered
A, B, …; a cross-reference to an appendix renders "Appendix A". See
<ref @app:notation> for the symbols used here.

<section | A second body section>

More body text, in section 2.

<appendix #app:notation | Notation>

The first appendix. With numbering on it is lettered "A", and a `<ref>` to it
reads "Appendix A".

<sub-section | Symbols>

A sub-section inside the appendix, numbered A.1.

<appendix | Further details>

A second appendix, lettered "B". The same `<appendix>` element works in a book,
where it lands in the back matter as a `<book-part>` instead.
